<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eannatum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2450 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/25th-century-bce">25th century BCE</a> · Also known as Eannatum of Lagash</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eannatum was a king of the Sumerian city-state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagash">Lagash</a> around 2450 BCE. He defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umma">Umma</a> in a long border war, commemorated on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stele-of-the-vultures">Stele of the Vultures</a>, and campaigned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kish">Kish</a>, Akshak, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>. He was among the rulers outside Kish who claimed the title 'king of Kish' to assert wider authority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eannatum.jpg" alt="Eannatum" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P1130735_Louvre_st%C3%A8le_des_Vautours_rwk.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
